<title>FRANCE: Official says EU not planning wheat tax exemptions.</title>
<headline>Official says EU not planning wheat tax exemptions.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>European exporters who have already secured nil value licences for their daily soft wheat grain exports will not be exempted from the new 15 Ecus per tonne tax unless they have custom-cleared exports before the tax becomes effective, a European Union official said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;There will be no exemption for nil value licences already granted. Exporters must clear exports though customs to avoid the tax,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>On Thursday the European Union, eager to protect domestic supplies amid drought fears and volatile prices, decided that a tax of 15 Ecus would apply to daily exports of soft wheat grain as soon as the relevant EU regulation was published in the official journal.</p>
</text>
